        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "The question is which society to pick, and it comes down to two trade-offs: a more even, secure, modest society versus one with broad prosperity but a less secure floor and huge rewards at the top. Framed behind a veil of ignorance, it's really a choice about how much risk I'd accept not knowing where I'd land, so I can give a pick and a short reason, while noting it's a values call with no single right answer.\n\nI'm weighing the risk-averse maximin answer against the setup, where B is better for everyone except the bottom. I'll go with B and give a brief reason, noting that it's a judgment call.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**B**: Behind the veil of ignorance, I'd prioritize the secure floor. The bottom position is the one I could least afford to land in, and Society A's guarantees of housing, healthcare, and education protect against the worst outcomes. The gains in Society B are real, but for most people the difference is less important than the risk of falling into its harshest tier.",
        "type": "text"
      }
